reset message. Editor runs need scene/plugin seed control; validate reset repeatability rather than assuming the Python argument reseeds Godot.","limitations","guidance","list","Setup","ordered",true,"items",[73,74,75],"setup","Install godot-rl in a Python environment and download a documented example such as JumperHard.","Use the matching Godot 4 .NET editor for the documented editor example; import the project.","Run the repository Stable Baselines 3 example, or adapt its environment interface to a fixed policy.","Try these tasks",false,[80,81,82],"testTasks","Change movement or reward logic, establish reset/replay repeatability for that scene, then compare fixed input rollouts.","Test sensors, action scaling and Python-to-game synchronization.","Replace a character or collider and verify that observations and control still work.","AI use and evaluation boundary","Designed for learning and automated gameplay testing. Keep imported-model rights and example attributions alongside the MIT toolkit license.","aiUseNote","links","Supporting evidence",[90,91,92],"evidence",{"_54":97,"_25":98},{"_54":95,"_25":96},{"_54":93,"_25":94},"Pinned binary-launch and reset seed behavior","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents/blob/207b6f476f5846f33d08b92c7a350147e7b78bf5/godot_rl/core/godot_env.py","Example asset attribution","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents#license","Editor and exported-game workflow","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents#quickstart-guide","Read the terms",[102],"licenseUrl",{"_54":99,"_25":103},"https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents/blob/main/LICENSE","Terms category","Mixed code / asset licenses","terms","provenance","Asset license","Example assets can have separate notices: the Cartoon Plane model is CC BY 4.0.","assetLicense","Code license","MIT for Godot RL Agents; Godot is also MIT.","codeLicense","Get started",[117],"access",{"_54":118,"_25":98,"_119":120},"Free toolkit and example projects","note","Install godot-rl a